WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.790
In 1970, airlines carried 310
million passengers worldwide.

2
00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:09.810
In 2019: 4.46 billion.

3
00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:15.090
Under the oceans, more than 600 active and
planned submarine cables carry international

4
00:00:15.140 --> 00:00:16.750
data traffic.

5
00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:23.130
Then, in January 2024, daily crossings
of the Panama Canal fell to a low of 27,

6
00:00:23.180 --> 00:00:26.410
against a long-term average of 38.

7
00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:29.950
So has technology really
made the world shrink?

8
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.110
Does distance no longer matter?

9
00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:35.230
In this mission, you'll
measure the shrinking world:

10
00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:39.570
time space convergence, air
travel, containers and data.

11
00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:43.050
Then you'll test resources,
distance and chokepoints,

12
00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:47.790
from cobalt in the Democratic Republic
of the Congo to the Strait of Hormuz.

13
00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:52.510
Your mission: evaluate whether technology
has really made the world shrink.
